00:54:08.300 --> 00:54:10.500
Come on. I need an answer!

808
00:54:12.500 --> 00:54:13.800
Calculations complete.

809
00:54:28.900 --> 00:54:31.400
You have a limit to your jump radius.
don't you?

810
00:54:32.200 --> 00:54:33.200
Thirty-three feet.

811
00:54:34.400 --> 00:54:36.400
I don't see anybody up here for you to hop
into.

812
00:54:37.800 --> 00:54:38.800
Very clever.

813
00:54:39.600 --> 00:54:43.400
Like I said. you're not getting near her.

814
00:54:58.300 --> 00:54:59.300
Hey. hey. hey. hey!

815
00:54:59.300 --> 00:54:59.700
I'm sorry. but you're in the wrong place.

816
00:54:59.700 --> 00:55:00.100
You're in danger.

817
00:55:00.200 --> 00:55:00.600
Where's your roommate?

818
00:55:00.700 --> 00:55:00.900
What?

819
00:55:01.100 --> 00:55:01.700
Where's Nick?

820
00:55:01.900 --> 00:55:03.000
I bossed it with friends.

821
00:55:03.100 --> 00:55:03.300
Why?

822
00:55:03.600 --> 00:55:03.900
Okay. good.

823
00:55:04.200 --> 00:55:04.900
You got a couple of things.

824
00:55:05.000 --> 00:55:05.100
What?

825
00:55:05.200 --> 00:55:07.200
I don't know if you're the real Spider-Man
or not coming with you.

826
00:55:07.200 --> 00:55:08.300
We don't have time for this.

827
00:55:08.300 --> 00:55:08.900
Please. come on.

828
00:55:09.000 --> 00:55:10.400
You need to get out of my apartment.

829
00:55:10.500 --> 00:55:12.200
Look. this is going to
sound insane. but there is

830
00:55:12.200 --> 00:55:14.300
someone who is after you
who is really dangerous. okay?

831
00:55:14.400 --> 00:55:16.200
And I promised you that I would keep you
safe.

832
00:55:17.300 --> 00:55:18.700
Please. you just have to trust me.

833
00:55:18.800 --> 00:55:19.800
Come on.

834
00:55:22.700 --> 00:55:23.700
Fine.

835
00:55:30.400 --> 00:55:31.400
Where would you stop?

836
00:55:35.200 --> 00:55:36.200
Where would you stop?

837
00:55:46.800 --> 00:55:47.400
Are you okay?

838
00:55:47.600 --> 00:55:48.200
Yeah. yeah. I'm fine.

839
00:55:48.500 --> 00:55:50.600
Okay. we should be safe up here.

840
00:01:12.200 --> 00:00:14.300
SUBS: CRETA STAR

841
00:52:30.700 --> 00:52:50.400
SUBS: CRETA STAR

842
02:24:28.100 --> 02:24:55.700
SUBS: CRETA STAR

843
00:55:51.200 --> 00:55:52.200
Okay. we'll see from what?

844
00:55:53.500 --> 00:55:54.500
Uh. I'm not entirely sure.

845
00:55:55.200 --> 00:55:56.700
Okay. well. what do they want with me?

846
00:55:56.800 --> 00:55:57.800
I don't know.

847
00:55:58.000 --> 00:55:59.000
You don't know?

848
00:55:59.700 --> 00:56:00.900
It doesn't make any sense.

849
00:56:01.000 --> 00:56:02.000
Why would they choose me?

850
00:56:02.400 --> 00:56:03.800
Um. I wish I could tell you.

851
00:56:03.900 --> 00:56:04.900
I just...

852
00:56:07.500 --> 00:56:08.700
We knew each other. didn't we?

853
00:56:12.700 --> 00:56:13.700
What?

854
00:56:14.800 --> 00:56:15.800
It's the only explanation.

855
00:56:17.400 --> 00:56:20.300
It's been driving me crazy for years.
all the times that Spider-Man saved.

856
00:56:20.500 --> 00:56:21.500
either me or Ned.

857
00:56:21.900 --> 00:56:23.500
It was the Washington
Monument. and then it

858
00:56:23.600 --> 00:56:25.600
was London. and Prague.
and the Night Monkey.

859
00:56:26.500 --> 00:56:28.800
I mean. twice is a coincidence.
but over and over again.

860
00:56:31.100 --> 00:56:32.100
We knew each other.

861
00:56:32.200 --> 00:56:33.200
Tell me I'm wrong.

862
00:56:35.300 --> 00:56:36.000
You're wrong.

863
00:56:36.300 --> 00:56:36.700
What were we?

864
00:56:36.800 --> 00:56:38.900
Were we classmates. or friends.
or something?

865
00:56:39.700 --> 00:56:41.600
Look. I don't know what you're talking
about.

866
00:56:42.100 --> 00:56:43.100
Were we something more?

867
00:56:45.500 --> 00:56:47.700
I just... I can't... I can't remember.

868
00:56:48.000 --> 00:56:52.200
And I feel like someone scrambled my brain.
and you're the only one who would know why.

869
00:56:52.700 --> 00:56:55.900
This is crazy. and I can't... I
know that you can't tell me the truth.

870
00:56:59.000 --> 00:57:00.000
But I need to know.

871
00:57:05.500 --> 00:57:07.400
Maybe there's a part of me that still
remembers.

872
00:57:52.300 --> 00:57:53.300
I hate the other.

873
00:57:59.600 --> 00:58:01.100
Oh. this is too much.

874
00:58:06.100 --> 00:58:08.100
I can't believe you figured it out.

875
00:58:08.700 --> 00:58:09.700
I did.

876
00:58:15.100 --> 00:58:16.100
Go ahead. Peter.

877
00:58:17.200 --> 00:58:18.200
Touch her.

878
00:58:19.100 --> 00:58:20.100
Hold her.

879
00:58:21.800 --> 00:58:23.400
You've been wanting to for so long.

880
00:58:32.100 --> 00:58:36.200
True love's kiss breaks the spell.
and reunites to serve cross-lovers.

881
00:58:38.700 --> 00:58:39.700
I'm David Vollman.

882
00:58:42.700 --> 00:58:44.400
You really are a simple spider.
aren't you?

883
00:58:45.200 --> 00:58:48.800
I see why you like her.

884
00:58:50.600 --> 00:58:52.700
She's. uh... She's smart.

885
00:58:55.600 --> 00:58:56.600
A little dark and twisted.

886
00:59:00.700 --> 00:59:01.700
I mean. it is sad.

887
00:59:03.100 --> 00:59:06.600
There is. like. no thoughts of you in
here.

888
00:59:07.700 --> 00:59:08.700
Whatsoever.

889
00:59:10.400 --> 00:59:11.600
But you knew that. didn't you?

890
00:59:12.800 --> 00:59:13.800
You're a monster.

891
00:59:15.300 --> 00:59:17.300
If you loved someone the
way that I love her. then you'd

892
00:59:17.300 --> 00:59:19.700
know that what you're doing
right now is unforgivable.

893
00:59:20.000 --> 00:59:21.000
Oh. is that so?

894
00:59:27.900 --> 00:59:31.100
You know. some people would kill to hold
the person they loved one last time.

895
00:59:33.200 --> 00:59:34.300
Stop it now.

896
00:59:42.200 --> 00:59:43.200
Oof.

897
00:59:44.300 --> 00:59:45.700
You're running out of time. Peter.

898
00:59:46.800 --> 00:59:49.900
Soon enough. it won't just be your friends
who don't remember Peter Parker.

899
00:59:51.800 --> 00:59:53.500
Maybe you should write a letter to
yourself.

900
00:59:57.600 --> 00:59:59.100
Get out of her.

901
01:00:00.600 --> 01:00:01.800
Who's the monster now. Peter?

902
01:00:11.500 --> 01:00:11.500
Oh!

903
01:00:11.600 --> 01:00:12.600
Oh!

904
01:00:12.700 --> 01:00:13.700
Oh!

905
01:00:23.300 --> 01:00:24.300
M.J.

906
01:00:26.300 --> 01:00:27.300
M.J.

907
01:00:27.500 --> 01:00:28.500
No. no. no.

908
01:00:28.600 --> 01:00:29.000
Oh. God.

909
01:00:29.500 --> 01:00:30.800
Oh. God. please. no. come on.

910
01:00:31.200 --> 01:00:32.200
Come on. come on. come

911
01:00:38.400 --> 01:00:38.600
on.

912
01:00:38.600 --> 01:00:39.600
Oh. I'm so sorry.

913
01:00:42.100 --> 01:00:43.100
Stop.

914
01:00:43.200 --> 01:00:44.300
Wait. wait. stop. stop. please.

915
01:00:44.300 --> 01:00:44.500
I'll quit.

916
01:00:44.700 --> 01:00:45.800
You win. you win. you win.

917
01:00:45.800 --> 01:00:46.800
Just don't hurt her.

918
01:00:49.600 --> 01:00:51.000
You're a mess. Spider-Man.

919
01:00:54.000 --> 01:00:55.000
Any time I want.

920
01:00:55.600 --> 01:00:56.800
I can be anyone I want.

921
01:00:58.200 --> 01:00:59.600
So you can't protect M.J.

922
01:01:01.200 --> 01:01:02.200
Even from herself.

923
01:01:10.400 --> 01:01:11.600
It really is a nice letter.

924
01:01:12.800 --> 01:01:13.800
A little heavy-handed.

925
01:01:14.100 --> 01:01:15.100
I'm not bad.

926
01:01:33.900 --> 01:01:34.900
You're okay.

927
01:01:35.200 --> 01:01:36.700
I'm gonna take you someplace safe.

928
01:01:36.900 --> 01:01:40.000
Take me to 3165.

929
01:01:40.300 --> 01:01:41.300
Lafayette Street.

930
01:01:41.900 --> 01:01:43.800
Navigating to Empire State University.

931
01:01:52.200 --> 01:01:53.200
I got you. I got you.

932
01:01:53.300 --> 01:01:53.500
You sure?

933
01:01:53.700 --> 01:01:53.900
Yep.

934
01:01:54.100 --> 01:01:55.500
Okay. because I feel like I'm slipping a
little bit.

935
01:01:55.600 --> 01:01:56.100
You're not slipping.

936
01:01:56.200 --> 01:01:57.200
Okay.

937
01:01:58.900 --> 01:02:00.400
You're okay. you're okay. you're okay.

938
01:02:00.500 --> 01:02:00.700
Yeah. yeah. yeah.

939
01:02:00.800 --> 01:02:01.800
I'm fine. I'm fine.

940
01:02:05.800 --> 01:02:08.500
Okay. can we just slow down for like two
seconds. please?

941
01:02:08.500 --> 01:02:09.000
We're almost there.

942
01:02:09.200 --> 01:02:11.400
Yeah. yeah. but you just told me I was
mind-controlled.

943
01:02:11.500 --> 01:02:12.000
Well. not technically.

944
01:02:12.100 --> 01:02:13.700
And you're lucky I believe in that stuff.
okay?

945
01:02:13.700 --> 01:02:16.500
Because governments have been doing it for
years. especially the French.

946
01:02:16.600 --> 01:02:17.000
Are you okay?

947
01:02:17.500 --> 01:02:20.100
Yeah. look. sorry. I'm just trying to take
you someplace safe. okay?

948
01:02:22.700 --> 01:02:25.800
Go. go. go. safe.

949
01:02:34.400 --> 01:02:35.400
Oh. watch out!

950
01:02:44.800 --> 01:02:45.900
You're losing it. kid.

951
01:02:46.700 --> 01:02:48.900
Thought you'd be able to see that coming a
mile away.

952
01:02:49.100 --> 01:02:50.200
What is wrong with you?

953
01:02:50.300 --> 01:02:51.200
You could have killed us.

954
01:02:51.200 --> 01:02:51.700
Excuse me?

955
01:02:52.100 --> 01:02:54.700
You show up to my house unannounced.
what do you think's gonna happen?

956
01:02:54.800 --> 01:02:55.600
Wait. this is your house?

957
01:02:55.700 --> 01:02:56.000
No. don't.

958
01:02:56.000 --> 01:02:57.000
Who the hell is that?

959
01:02:57.300 --> 01:02:58.300
Who the hell are you?

960
01:02:59.000 --> 01:03:01.800
She's. um. you know.

961
01:03:02.200 --> 01:03:02.900
No. I don't know.

962
01:03:03.000 --> 01:03:04.100
That's why I just asked you.

963
01:03:04.400 --> 01:03:05.500
She's in danger. Frank.

964
01:03:05.600 --> 01:03:06.800
Look. I need your help. okay?

965
01:03:07.100 --> 01:03:08.100
Yeah. looks like it.

966
01:03:08.100 --> 01:03:09.200
Well. come on. you owe me.

967
01:03:09.600 --> 01:03:10.200
Ah. for Christ's sake.

968
01:03:10.200 --> 01:03:11.400
What's your sickest story?

969
01:03:11.700 --> 01:03:12.000
Staten Island.

970
01:03:12.500 --> 01:03:13.500
Nah. Staten Island.

971
01:03:13.600 --> 01:03:14.800
What more do you want me to do?

972
01:03:14.800 --> 01:03:16.200
I literally saved your life.

973
01:03:16.200 --> 01:03:17.300
You're out of your mind. kid.

974
01:03:17.400 --> 01:03:19.100
Well. I gotta save it twice to get a favor
out of you.

975
01:03:19.100 --> 01:03:20.800
That guy could hit me with a handful of
rice.

976
01:03:20.800 --> 01:03:21.800
What does that sound like to you?

977
01:03:21.800 --> 01:03:23.600
I had an exact amount of sugar on one of
them.

978
01:03:23.600 --> 01:03:24.500
I see them right there.

979
01:03:24.500 --> 01:03:26.700
I know exactly what I'm talking to you.

980
01:03:27.400 --> 01:03:28.100
Okay. fine. go ahead.

981
01:03:28.300 --> 01:03:28.700
What would you call that?

982
01:03:28.700 --> 01:03:30.000
What does that sound like to you?

983
01:03:31.000 --> 01:03:32.400
I don't care. I just wanna go home.

984
01:03:33.100 --> 01:03:34.400
That's an excellent idea.

985
01:03:34.800 --> 01:03:35.400
Kick rocks. go home.

986
01:03:35.400 --> 01:03:37.200
No. no. wait. wait. wait. wait.
wait. wait. wait. wait. wait.

987
01:03:37.200 --> 01:03:38.200
Please.

988
01:03:39.300 --> 01:03:40.900
Hey. I've got to keep her safe.
okay?

989
01:03:41.000 --> 01:03:42.500
And I don't have anywhere else to go.

990
01:03:46.700 --> 01:03:47.700
You like chili?

991
01:03:49.100 --> 01:03:50.100
I made chili.

992
01:03:51.900 --> 01:03:54.800
All right. just watch out for the
claymores.

993
01:03:55.300 --> 01:03:57.400
I won't pick up pieces at you for the next
two weeks.

994
01:03:59.100 --> 01:04:00.900
Hey. I definitely would not eat that
chili.

995
01:04:03.100 --> 01:04:05.400
So you're telling me
that maniac behind all that

996
01:04:05.400 --> 01:04:08.000
tank nonsense is nothing
but a goddamn teenager.

997
01:04:08.300 --> 01:04:11.700
And it's not just a tank. it's every
attack on damage control this past month.

998
01:04:12.100 --> 01:04:13.900
How does a kid learn how to drive a tank?

999
01:04:14.100 --> 01:04:15.100
I don't know. Frank.

1000
01:04:15.300 --> 01:04:17.000
Beat your ass all over the street like
that.

1001
01:04:17.000 --> 01:04:18.000
She did not beat my ass.

1002
01:04:18.900 --> 01:04:19.900
Is this your family?

1003
01:04:23.400 --> 01:04:24.900
You should get the hell away from that.

1004
01:04:25.800 --> 01:04:27.400
Look. I got one rule in this house.

1005
01:04:28.000 --> 01:04:30.700
You don't touch anything. you don't move
anything.

1006
01:04:30.700 --> 01:04:33.800
You sure as shit don't ask me any goddamn
questions about anything.

1007
01:04:35.400 --> 01:04:36.400
It's the three rules.

1008
01:04:39.800 --> 01:04:41.200
I see why you like her.

1009
01:04:42.200 --> 01:04:43.300
Go put some pants on.

1010
01:04:45.100 --> 01:04:46.100
Don't touch the chili.

1011
01:04:48.100 --> 01:04:49.100
I like him.

1012
01:04:50.400 --> 01:04:51.400
Of course you do.

1013
01:04:52.700 --> 01:04:56.200
So I managed to pull this image from my
HUD and run it through the system.

1014
01:04:59.100 --> 01:05:00.200
Who is she?

1015
01:05:00.800 --> 01:05:01.800
Until a couple months ago.

1016
01:05:02.400 --> 01:05:03.400
Nobody.

1017
01:05:04.200 --> 01:05:06.400
She was in and out of foster
care. psych hospitals. and

1018
01:05:06.400 --> 01:05:08.600
then eventually she ran
away and dropped off the grid.

1019
01:05:09.000 --> 01:05:10.900
It's hardly any information about
her that hasn't been scrubbed.

1020
01:05:10.900 --> 01:05:14.600
but she's classified as a
telepath. and now we have a name.

1021
01:05:18.300 --> 01:05:19.300
Jean Grey.

1022
01:05:21.000 --> 01:05:22.000
Yeah.

1023
01:05:22.300 --> 01:05:24.600
These are the damage control sites that
she hasn't hit yet.

1024
01:05:25.100 --> 01:05:28.600
So if she surfaces. then my facial
tracking program will pick her up.

1025
01:05:29.700 --> 01:05:30.000
Right.

1026
01:05:30.700 --> 01:05:31.100
Oh. yeah.

1027
01:05:31.500 --> 01:05:32.500
What then?

1028
01:05:34.600 --> 01:05:36.000
Well. don't worry about what then.

1029
01:05:36.200 --> 01:05:37.200
Just look after her.

1030
01:05:37.300 --> 01:05:38.400
Don't worry about it. huh?

1031
01:05:39.000 --> 01:05:41.300
I'm just supposed to sit here and babysit
your girlfriend.

1032
01:05:41.500 --> 01:05:44.700
She's not my girlfriend. so... All
right. look. what's the plan. huh?

1033
01:05:45.200 --> 01:05:49.000
You just gotta hope that your facial
tracking program works. and you get

1034
01:05:49.000 --> 01:05:51.100
yourself killed. I gotta watch her the
rest of my life.

1035
01:05:51.100 --> 01:05:52.500
I'm not gonna get killed. Frank.

1036
01:05:52.600 --> 01:05:53.500
I can catch her. okay?

1037
01:05:53.500 --> 01:05:56.800
I just have to fix my inhibitor.
and then I'll be good to go.

1038
01:05:57.500 --> 01:05:58.700
What do you need to do that?

1039
01:06:00.200 --> 01:06:03.700
Frank. you do not have what I need to do
that. okay?

1040
01:06:05.300 --> 01:06:06.800
You've got some mouth on you.

1041
01:06:06.900 --> 01:06:10.400
What. do you think you have an anti-static
mat. a tonal probe. and micro-tools?

1042
01:06:11.300 --> 01:06:12.300
I got all that shit.

1043
01:06:13.400 --> 01:06:14.400
What for?

1044
01:06:14.500 --> 01:06:14.700
Bombs.

1045
01:06:15.200 --> 01:06:16.200
Bingo.

1046
01:06:18.700 --> 01:06:19.700
Unbelievable.

1047
01:06:31.200 --> 01:06:34.600
Hey. do you think it's safe to maybe call
someone and let them know I'm okay?

1048
01:06:39.100 --> 01:06:40.100
Uh... like your boyfriend?

1049
01:06:41.900 --> 01:06:43.500
No. like my roommate.

1050
01:06:46.800 --> 01:06:47.800
Oh. um...

1051
01:06:48.000 --> 01:06:49.900
I don't think that's such a good idea.
you know?

1052
01:06:49.900 --> 01:06:54.600
Because she already knows who he is.
and she can inhabit anyone she wants.

1053
01:06:54.800 --> 01:06:56.000
so... Right. yeah.

1054
01:06:56.300 --> 01:06:57.500
Yeah. yeah. yeah. you're right.

1055
01:06:57.800 --> 01:06:58.100
Sorry.

1056
01:06:58.500 --> 01:06:59.000
No. it's fine.

1057
01:06:59.200 --> 01:07:00.500
I totally get it.

1058
01:07:02.400 --> 01:07:06.800
If I call my boyfriend. he'd just ask me a
bunch of questions that I couldn't answer.

1059
01:07:07.000 --> 01:07:10.200
and he'd tell me I was being withholding
again.

1060
01:07:10.600 --> 01:07:10.900
Withholding?

1061
01:07:11.400 --> 01:07:12.400
Yep.

1062
01:07:12.500 --> 01:07:14.300
Sounds like your boyfriend's kind of a
jerk.

1063
01:07:17.100 --> 01:07:18.500
Why do you think you're withholding?

1064
01:07:19.100 --> 01:07:20.100
I don't know.

1065
01:07:20.400 --> 01:07:22.800
He'd tell me mass vigilante behind the
curtain.

1066
01:07:25.200 --> 01:07:26.600
Um... okay. I see your point.

1067
01:07:28.700 --> 01:07:29.700
So what about you?

1068
01:07:30.500 --> 01:07:31.500
What about me?

